body:
I have a couple of other iterations in for @clayjohn and @SoftLattice to try on NVIDIA / AMD hardware out of curiosity.

My results are that `new_alt.glsl` is faster and more accurate on Apple Silicon. Curious how it performs on discrete GPUs.

| name | image |
| :---- | :---- |
| copy.glsl | <img width="80%" alt="CleanShot 2026-08-26 at 14 50 02@2x" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d6838ec-cfbe-40eb-89e1-2e9bac823614" /> |
| new_alt.glsl | <img width="80%" alt="CleanShot 2026-08-26 at 14 50 50@2x" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d92e71e-8014-45c6-b9f4-20853032bde9" /> |



